WEBVTT

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:58.830
<i>I am pleased to have met you again, my beloved princess...</i>

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:02.800
<i>Um...</i>

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:05.590
<i>I've been meaning to thank you...</i>

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:11.460
<i>Because of you, I found something incredibly important to me.</i>

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.400
<i>I should be the one thanking you.</i>

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.150
<i>What?</i>

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:21.110
<i>The songs you spin saved me.</i>

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.060
<i>I have been waiting for this day.</i>

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:31.790
<i>I've wanted to touch you, Haruka.</i>

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.370
<i>Um, I...</i>

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.910
A dream?

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:20.110
Shining, I've got work to do.

00:03:20.110 --> 00:03:22.160
You're such a demanding boss.

00:03:22.160 --> 00:03:26.680
In any case, please cut that paper quickly!

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.640
Um, did you call me?

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:36.230
Oh, I've been waiting for you, Miss Nanami.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:42.850
I know it's soon, but you will compose a new song for ST☆RISH.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:43.740
What?!

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.530
That's great. He's asking you to write a new song?

00:03:47.530 --> 00:03:54.830
Write a song like "Maji LOVE 1000%" that I'll want to listen to again and again.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:04:02.470
Okay. I'll try to write a song that will make listeners feel happy.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.550
<i>Songs that will make the listeners feel happy, huh?</i>

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:13.580
Work hard, Haru. You made those six into a single group.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.270
I'm sure you'll be able to write something amazing.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:20.730
What? Actually, I didn't come up with that song.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.260
What do you mean?

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:27.490
I met a prince in my dreams who taught it to me.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.910
Never mind!

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:34.530
Haru, you're such a romantic.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:38.740
But there are some pushy princes out there, so be careful.

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:39.560
What?

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.680
You're the only girl in the dorm.

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:45.920
I look forward to hearing your new song, Miss Nanami.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:51.140
Spin lots of songs that will turn the world upside down.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:53.810
Okay.

00:04:57.290 --> 00:05:02.710
<i>The songs you spin saved me.</i>

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.420
<i>I should be the one thanking you.</i>

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.680
<i>I have been waiting for this day.</i>

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.660
Cecil, you...

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.950
Jinguji, your choreography was lazy in the middle.

00:05:22.950 --> 00:05:24.390
Really?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:28.730
It feels so nice to practice first thing in the morning, doesn't it, Shou?

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.090
I'm so hungry I feel like I'm going to die.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.310
Me too...

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.470
This song...

00:06:11.410 --> 00:06:12.170
Nanami?

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.490
What a warm voice.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.060
We finally meet, Haruka.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.870
Cecil!

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:33.080
Cecil, is this a dream too?

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:37.930
This is not a dream, my princess...

00:07:38.370 --> 00:07:40.860
From now on, I will be by your side always.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:45.790
You!

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:47.430
What do you think you're doing to Nanami?!

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:54.950
Haruka, I have been waiting a long time to touch you like this.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:57.540
What?! C-Cecil!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.580
Get away from Nanami!

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.580
Enough! Who the heck is this guy?!

00:08:03.060 --> 00:08:04.880
Nanami, do you know him?

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:09.320
Well, we've met a few times in my dreams...

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:15.690
This voice!

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.690
President, when did you get here?!

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:24.200
Allow me to introduce you.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:32.730
His name is Aijima Cecil. He is the Prince of Agnapolis, the land of music.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:36.570
He's a real-life prince, he is.

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:38.620
A prince?!

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.280
What is he doing here?!

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.750
I scouted him.

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:46.400
What?

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:55.310
That's right. Starting today, Mr. Aijima is a member

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.560
of the Master Course, just like you.

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:05.960
Boys and girls, play nicely together.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:11.220
I've got a meeting, so... Bye, bye, bye!

00:09:14.210 --> 00:09:18.480
Cecil is joining the Master Course...

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.090
I told you...

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:24.820
I will be by your side from now on...

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:38.380
Everyone, let's welcome our guest from a distant land.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:41.670
I even made my special, homemade cookies.

00:09:44.980 --> 00:09:47.060
What's wrong, everyone?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:49.650
I'm surprised you can accept this so easily.

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:52.750
Why do we have to welcome him, anyway?

00:09:53.090 --> 00:09:57.420
What? Well, if Cecil is going to be a member of the Master Course,

00:09:58.070 --> 00:09:59.660
we should try to be friends with him.

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.780
Let's introduce ourselves. I'm—

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:05.270
Shinomiya Natsuki.

00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:06.360
What?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:12.570
Your hobby is cooking. You like tea and cookies.

00:10:13.390 --> 00:10:15.000
How do you know that?

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.380
Do you know Shinomiya?

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:22.970
No, but I can tell by looking at his eyes.

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:27.550
Your heart is warm and kind, like a sunny spot.

00:10:28.060 --> 00:10:30.690
Your warmth heals the hearts of those around you.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.370
I'm so pleased to hear you say that.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:40.130
And someday, the darkness you keep locked away in your heart will disappear.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:43.980
How do you know so much about Natsuki?

00:10:43.980 --> 00:10:47.370
I know a lot about you as well, Ittoki Otoya.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.110
Me?

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:53.990
You treasure the smiles of others above all else.

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:55.480
Their smiles?

00:10:56.350 --> 00:11:00.480
Your songs will surely continue to evolve.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.320
S-Seriously?!

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.610
You're just making things up.

00:11:04.610 --> 00:11:09.350
Kurusu Shou, your body may be small, but you are very athletic.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:10.760
D-Don't call me small!

00:11:11.550 --> 00:11:13.420
The contrast between your cute looks

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:16.730
and masculine personality is your appeal.

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.910
Shou, isn't it great to be complimented?

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:20.740
However...

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:25.430
Your violent temperament causes conflicts with others.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:27.160
He's right.

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:29.210
Who are you?

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:30.900
Hijirikawa Masato.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.350
You seem calm, cool, and collected,

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:37.880
but you hide a massive feeling on the verge of exploding within yourself.

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:41.290
What are you hiding?

00:11:42.490 --> 00:11:44.080
Ichinose Tokiya.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:47.440
Songs are a mirror that reflect the heart.

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:51.500
You are already heading towards the next stage.

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.020
Well, well...

00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.390
You're like a fortune teller.

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:56.680
Jinguji Ren.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:11:58.670
Thanks, but I'll pass.

00:11:58.670 --> 00:12:00.030
Why not do it?

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.140
Why not have him tell you your future too?

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:07.240
Soon, the chains in your heart will disappear.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:11.820
You will feel happy from the bottom of your heart.

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:13.550
This is amazing!

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:15.960
You really understand us!

00:12:17.660 --> 00:12:21.290
Hey, wait! Don't tell me you believe this guy!

00:12:23.090 --> 00:12:23.960
Um...

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:28.920
Actually, when we had to choose partners for the graduation audition,

00:12:29.380 --> 00:12:34.310
Cecil was the one who advised me to choose all of you.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:36.130
Wh-What did you say?

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:39.240
You didn't make the decision by yourself?

00:12:39.240 --> 00:12:44.010
Then, if not for him, ST☆RISH would never have formed...

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.740
He's not just some weird foreign student.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.620
He's the person who brought us together.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:55.430
So please, have some faith in Cecil.

00:12:56.920 --> 00:13:00.340
So, what are you going to do in the Master Course?

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.310
Do you want to become an idol?

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:04.420
I am not interested in becoming an idol.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:05.460
What?

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:07.870
I simply want to be with Haruka.

00:13:09.280 --> 00:13:13.840
I wish to combine my poetry with the music you create and sing.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.550
You want her to compose music and sing?

00:13:16.550 --> 00:13:20.740
Is that the only reason you entered the Shining Agency?

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:27.360
Yes. The goddesses of music, the muses, live in your music.

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:31.750
My family has been serving the muses for generations.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:36.330
Haruka's music guided me here.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:41.640
I am best suited to singing your songs.

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.040
You!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:47.480
My princess, Haruka. I love you.

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:51.210
Huh? Wh-What?!

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.320
What?!

00:13:51.820 --> 00:13:54.650
Is that all right, Haruka?

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.050
No, no!

00:13:57.180 --> 00:13:59.050
You jerk!

00:13:59.330 --> 00:14:01.840
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.150
Don't be ridiculous!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.060
Shut up, you fools!

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.700
To speak so boldly of love in this Master Course...

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:12.570
You are fools!

00:14:15.370 --> 00:14:17.140
Wh-What's going on?!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:24.180
I am the Count of the Silk Palace from the country of Permafrost!

00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:31.180
I am a knight in service of the queen!

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:35.460
I am the idol of ancient and honorable origin, Camus!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.810
First a prince, and now a count?

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:43.720
Hold your tongue, fool.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:45.700
Are you Aijima?

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:50.100
Be grateful. Starting today, I am assigned to you.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:53.100
Oh, right. Cecil has his own senior.

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:55.090
A senior...

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:57.440
I have no need for one of those.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.870
I am not interested in becoming an idol.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:04.680
I do not understand why Saotome allowed you to enter the Master Course...

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.190
But here, senior and junior relationships are absolute.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.950
You will respect me and study show business.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:13.680
Understood?

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:15.500
No.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:23.470
You seem to wish to sing this girl's songs.

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:25.110
Do you really believe you can sing a professional's songs

00:15:25.630 --> 00:15:27.750
when you can't even grasp the fundamentals of being an idol?

00:15:29.230 --> 00:15:33.530
An amateur like yourself cannot compare to a professional!

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:35.710
That's not true.

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:40.450
Because the muses smile on me, I can sing better than anyone else...

00:15:40.450 --> 00:15:42.420
Even better than the members of ST☆RISH!

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:44.360
Better than us?

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.590
That's some confidence.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:50.530
Very well. Come outside.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:55.000
These are the president's special, idol training cards.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.220
Idol training...

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:58.170
Karuta?

00:15:58.560 --> 00:15:59.440
They're huge.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:03.690
Compete against ST☆RISH using these, and show us just how good you are.

00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.480
Compete?

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.110
Looks like they're doing something interesting.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:11.120
Rei?

00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:15.850
It's one of the training exercises for people new to the Master Course.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.560
A battle between amateurs...

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:20.580
He's a perfect match for you.

00:16:21.130 --> 00:16:24.880
Why are we playing karuta, anyway? Shouldn't we compete by singing?

00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:27.220
Everything begins with fundamentals.

00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:30.700
You are far too inexperienced to be battling with songs!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:37.530
Isn't there a better way to test our fundamentals?

00:16:36.370 --> 00:16:39.040
Don't worry about the small stuff!

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.630
What's wrong?

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:44.480
Have you lost your nerve because it is not a contest of songs?

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.020
You can still turn back now.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:50.840
No, I will win.

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:53.510
I will win and prove my love for Haruka!

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:53.990
What?

00:16:54.230 --> 00:16:56.200
That jerk!

00:16:56.200 --> 00:17:00.080
Shou, aren't these karuta cards so big and exciting?

00:17:00.080 --> 00:17:01.830
This isn't a game!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:05.010
We'll have to give this everything we have.

00:17:05.010 --> 00:17:06.000
It seems that way.

00:17:06.590 --> 00:17:07.940
We have to do it.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:09.670
We won't hold back.

00:17:10.080 --> 00:17:11.460
Bring it on.

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:13.980
Woman, you will read the cards.

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:14.910
Okay.

00:17:17.350 --> 00:17:19.750
Your time limit is thirty minutes!

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:22.280
Begin!

00:17:22.610 --> 00:17:27.020
"First class recklessness, idols give everything they can!"

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:28.260
All right!

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.260
Got it!

00:17:33.090 --> 00:17:34.200
What?!

00:17:38.900 --> 00:17:41.820
This is "mu," is it not?

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:42.800
You're kidding!

00:17:42.800 --> 00:17:45.640
My hiragana is perfect.

00:17:45.970 --> 00:17:48.880
"Always enjoy everything with a smile!"

00:17:49.130 --> 00:17:52.010
"All eyes on idols!"

00:17:52.430 --> 00:17:56.010
"A little carelessness can be dangerous!"

00:17:58.420 --> 00:17:59.950
I did it.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:01.510
What's going on?

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.720
Is the newbie going to win by himself?

00:18:04.210 --> 00:18:05.590
He's good.

00:18:05.590 --> 00:18:06.570
Yes.

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:09.010
Cecil's super fast.

00:18:09.010 --> 00:18:10.900
No, wait. This is...

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.870
Not "i," but "ko"!

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:17.340
This isn't "shi," but "tsu"!

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.990
This isn't "chi," but "sa"...

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:23.140
They look kind of similar.

00:18:23.590 --> 00:18:26.040
You jerk, you got all the wrong cards!

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:27.080
What?!

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.500
I am disappointed....

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.000
I was so confident in my Japanese!

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.490
How?

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:35.990
I will get the right card this time!

00:18:37.460 --> 00:18:38.990
That was a quick turnaround.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.490
An idol has got to be that way.

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.500
Let's go!

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.790
"Luck and talent are both important!"

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:47.230
All right!

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.520
"U"! Where is it?

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.040
"U"! "U"! Where is it?

00:18:56.330 --> 00:18:57.030
Oh, no!

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.010
It's way over there!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.250
This one is mine.

00:19:05.590 --> 00:19:07.830
Oh, no, you don't!

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.050
Shou!

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:18.760
Huh?

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:23.200
W-Water!

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:24.970
No!

00:19:34.950 --> 00:19:37.070
H-Help me! Someone, help!

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:38.820
Your feet should touch the bottom.

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:41.260
What?

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.730
That was great! You're awesome, newbie!

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:53.430
You're so mean. I can't believe no one tried to save me...

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.310
A fish!

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.510
I've had enough of this!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:05.840
He's dropping out.

00:20:06.220 --> 00:20:08.310
Seriously? But why?!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:10.770
According to my data, he comes from the desert.

00:20:11.450 --> 00:20:13.530
He doesn't like water or fish.

00:20:13.530 --> 00:20:14.770
What?!

00:20:16.150 --> 00:20:18.260
He was all talk.

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:23.030
What a ridiculous day.

00:20:23.230 --> 00:20:25.660
I wonder where Cecil went.

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:27.490
Who cares?

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:29.160
Cecil!

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:30.870
This guy!

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:33.280
He's asleep.

00:20:33.280 --> 00:20:36.010
The fundamentals of an idol? These are easy.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.210
Aijima!

00:20:40.810 --> 00:20:43.130
First, you ran away, and now you're napping...

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:46.900
You're so noisy, Camus.

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:50.960
And you're supposed to be a count. Don't make me laugh.

00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.820
You...

00:20:53.820 --> 00:20:56.900
Unforgivable! Wake up!

00:20:57.640 --> 00:21:01.280
Camus? Why are you shouting?

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.230
Aijima!

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:06.310
I will pound some sense into that rotten head of yours! Come!

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:08.530
L-Let go of me!

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:10.740
What did I do?

00:21:11.090 --> 00:21:12.610
Camus!

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:14.010
Quit complaining!

00:21:14.010 --> 00:21:17.200
An unbelievable kid has come into our midst.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:23.680
But who knows how that training would have concluded if we had continued.

00:21:23.680 --> 00:21:26.610
Cecil has the right character.

00:21:26.610 --> 00:21:29.720
But he's not interested in becoming an idol, right?

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:48.090
Cecil, um...

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:54.030
Because I lost the contest, I will obey Camus.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:58.560
He told me romantic relationships are forbidden here.

00:21:59.030 --> 00:22:02.190
I allowed you to see an embarrassing side of myself.

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:03.920
Not at all!

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:10.840
Cecil, are you really not interested in becoming an idol?

00:22:12.100 --> 00:22:15.030
The song you sang today was wonderful...

00:22:15.440 --> 00:22:20.530
For me, singing is as natural as breathing.

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:23.330
It differs slightly from the songs of an idol.

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:29.990
My desire is to sing songs you have written for me.

00:22:31.380 --> 00:22:33.660
That is all.

00:24:06.500 --> 00:24:08.210
Show your support for QUARTET NIGHT too!

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:09.140
Ready, and...

00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:10.310
Uta Pri!
